#X text 240 83 Reads and writes data over a serial port. The object
can send byte values to a connected device (as a single float or as
a list of floats in the [0 \, 255] range) and outputs each byte received
from the port. The port and baud rate can be set with arguments or
properties \, the list of available serial devices is available in
@devices.;
#X text 240 199 Typical use cases:;
#X text 250 224 • Arduino and microcontroller control — sending and
receiving byte commands from an Arduino \, Teensy or similar board
\, for example to drive motors \, relays or LEDs \, or to read sensor
values.;
#X text 250 294 • Hardware synthesizers and MIDI interfaces — communicating
with devices that use serial protocols \, for example some older synthesizers
\, DMX controllers or custom hardware over USB-serial converters.;
